{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NFKGnmLUCEBwEEatUCWudj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Token-based hash table.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Replaces the C `picohash_table` (an open-addressed table with\n4\t//! chained collision lists, intrusive `picohash_item`s embedded in\n5\t//! the caller's structs and a function-pointer trio for hashing /\n6\t//! comparing / projecting the embedded item).\n7\t//!\n8\t//! ## API shape\n9\t//!\n10\t//! `HashTable<K, V>` is a slotmap-backed hash map.  `K: Hash + Eq`\n11\t//! provides the key contract; `V` is whatever the caller stores\n12\t//! (usually a token into some other arena — see Phase-4 plan\n13\t//! below).  The trio of C function pointers is gone: hashing comes\n14\t//! from `K`'s `Hash` impl, comparison from `Eq`, and the table\n15\t//! never reaches into the caller's struct so no `key_to_item`\n16\t//! callback is needed.\n17\t//!\n18\t//! Operations return [`HashToken`]s — opaque (`idx, generation`)\n19\t//! handles into this table's slot vector.  Tokens are `Copy`,\n20\t//! survive insertion and removal of *other* keys, but become stale\n21\t//! the moment the keyed entry is removed (the slot's generation\n22\t//! bumps).  [`HashTable::get`] returns `None` for stale tokens —\n23\t//! the safe equivalent of the C dangling-`HashItem*` use-after-free.\n24\t//!\n25\t//! ## Phase 4 plan — implementation\n26\t//!\n27\t//! The bodies in this module are `todo!()`.  Phase 4 picks one of:\n28\t//!\n29\t//! 1. **Hand-roll the slotmap.**  Internal layout (illustrative):\n30\t//!\n31\t//!    ```ignore\n32\t//!    struct Slot<K, V> {\n33\t//!        generation: u32,\n34\t//!        state: SlotState<K, V>,\n35\t//!    }\n36\t//!    enum SlotState<K, V> {\n37\t//!        Free   { next_free: Option<u32> },\n38\t//!        Filled { hash: u64, key: K, value: V, next_in_bin: Option<u32> },\n39\t//!    }\n40\t//!    pub struct HashTable<K, V> {\n41\t//!        slots: Vec<Slot<K, V>>,\n42\t//!        free:  Option<u32>,\n43\t//!        bins:  Vec<Option<u32>>,\n44\t//!        seed:  [u8; 16],\n45\t//!        len:   usize,\n46\t//!    }\n47\t//!    ```\n48\t//!\n49\t//!    `next_in_bin` lives inside the slot, not the user struct, so\n50\t//!    no `unsafe`.  Lookup hashes `K` to a bin index, walks the\n51\t//!    chain by following `next_in_bin` slot indices, comparing each\n52\t//!    `slot.key` against the target.  Insert pushes a new slot\n53\t//!    (or pops one off the free list) and threads it onto the bin\n54\t//!    chain.  Remove unlinks, marks the slot `Free`, bumps\n55\t//!    generation, and adds it to the free list.\n56\t//!\n57\t//! 2. **Build on the `slotmap` crate.**  `slotmap::SlotMap` already\n58\t//!    provides the slot/generation/free-list machinery; this module\n59\t//!    layers the bin-array indexing on top.  The crate is\n60\t//!    `no_std`-friendly with the right features and would let us\n61\t//!    delete maybe 80% of the implementation.\n62\t//!\n63\t//! Either implementation should keep `HashToken` byte-compatible\n64\t//! with the public API below — the choice is local.\n65\t//!\n66\t//! ## Phase 4 plan — call sites\n67\t//!\n68\t//! In the C tree, every hash table is intrusive: the value type\n69\t//! embeds a `HashItem` field and the table's bins point straight\n70\t//! into the middle of those user-owned objects.  In the Rust port\n71\t//! the embedding turns into a *membership token*: the parent\n72\t//! struct holds `Option<HashToken>` for each table it can be in,\n73\t//! and the table's slot stores the parent's `ConnectionToken`\n74\t//! (or other token type) into the arena that owns the parent.\n75\t//!\n76\t//! For example, `quic.connection_by_id: HashTable<ConnectionId,\n77\t//! ConnectionToken>` points at connections that live in\n78\t//! `quic.connections: Arena<Connection>`.  A `Connection` carries\n79\t//! `connection_by_id_membership: Option<HashToken>`; on removal the\n80\t//! Connection hands that token back for an O(1) `connection_by_id.remove`.\n81\t\n82\textern crate alloc;\n83\tuse alloc::vec::Vec;\n84\t\n85\tuse core::hash::{Hash, Hasher};\n86\t\n87\tuse crate::Error;\n88\t\n89\t/// Opaque handle into a [`HashTable`]'s slot vector.\n90\t///\n91\t/// `idx` selects a slot; `generation` is incremented on every\n92\t/// removal so an old token comparing against a recycled slot\n93\t/// returns `None` from [`HashTable::get`].  The pair is `Copy` and\n94\t/// 64-bit total — call sites pass it by value.\n95\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]\n96\tpub struct HashToken {\n97\t    idx: u32,\n98\t    generation: u32,\n99\t}\n100\t\n101\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n102\t// Internal slot storage\n103\t\n104\tstruct Slot<K, V> {\n105\t    generation: u32,\n106\t    state: SlotState<K, V>,\n107\t}\n108\t\n109\tenum SlotState<K, V> {\n110\t    Free {\n111\t        next_free: Option<u32>,\n112\t    },\n113\t    Filled {\n114\t        hash: u64,\n115\t        key: K,\n116\t        value: V,\n117\t        next_in_bin: Option<u32>,\n118\t    },\n119\t}\n120\t\n121\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n122\t// Seeded hasher — streams bytes through the picohash_bytes mixing function.\n123\t\n124\tstruct SeedHasher {\n125\t    hash: u64,\n126\t    rotate: u32,\n127\t    seed: [u8; 16],\n128\t    byte_idx: u32,\n129\t}\n130\t\n131\timpl SeedHasher {\n132\t    fn new(seed: &[u8; 16]) -> Self {\n133\t        let hash = u64::from_le_bytes(seed[8..16].try_into().unwrap());\n134\t        SeedHasher {\n135\t            hash,\n136\t            rotate: 11,\n137\t            seed: *seed,\n138\t            byte_idx: 0,\n139\t        }\n140\t    }\n141\t}\n142\t\n143\timpl Hasher for SeedHasher {\n144\t    fn write(&mut self, bytes: &[u8]) {\n145\t        for &b in bytes {\n146\t            self.hash ^= b as u64;\n147\t            self.hash ^= self.seed[(self.byte_idx & 15) as usize] as u64;\n148\t            self.hash ^= self.hash << 8;\n149\t            self.hash = self.hash.wrapping_add(self.hash >> self.rotate);\n150\t            self.rotate = (self.hash & 31) as u32 + 11;\n151\t            self.byte_idx = self.byte_idx.wrapping_add(1);\n152\t        }\n153\t    }\n154\t\n155\t    fn finish(&self) -> u64 {\n156\t        let mut h = self.hash;\n157\t        h ^= h >> self.rotate;\n158\t        h\n159\t    }\n160\t}\n161\t\n162\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n163\t\n164\t/// Hash table mapping `K` to `V`, addressable by [`HashToken`].\n165\t///\n166\t/// The value `V` is typically a token into some other arena (see\n167\t/// the Phase-4 call-site plan in the module docs) but any owned\n168\t/// value works.  `K: Hash + Eq` is the only contract on the key.\n169\tpub struct HashTable<K, V> {\n170\t    slots: Vec<Slot<K, V>>,\n171\t    free: Option<u32>,\n172\t    bins: Vec<Option<u32>>,\n173\t    seed: [u8; 16],\n174\t    len: usize,\n175\t}\n176\t\n177\timpl<K: Hash + Eq, V> HashTable<K, V> {\n178\t    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n179\t    // Constructors\n180\t\n181\t    /// Build an empty table with `nb_bin` collision bins, using a\n182\t    /// zero hash seed.\n183\t    ///\n184\t    /// C: `picohash_create`.\n185\t    pub fn new(nb_bin: usize) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n186\t        Self::with_seed(nb_bin, &[0u8; 16])\n187\t    }\n188\t\n189\t    /// Like [`HashTable::new`] but with a caller-supplied 16-byte\n190\t    /// hash seed.\n191\t    ///\n192\t    /// C: `picohash_create_ex`.\n193\t    pub fn with_seed(nb_bin: usize, hash_seed: &[u8; 16]) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n194\t        let bins = alloc::vec![None; nb_bin];\n195\t        Ok(Self {\n196\t            slots: Vec::new(),\n197\t            free: None,\n198\t            bins,\n199\t            seed: *hash_seed,\n200\t            len: 0,\n201\t        })\n202\t    }\n203\t\n204\t    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n205\t    // Internal helpers\n206\t\n207\t    fn hash_key(&self, key: &K) -> u64 {\n208\t        let mut h = SeedHasher::new(&self.seed);\n209\t        key.hash(&mut h);\n210\t        h.finish()\n211\t    }\n212\t\n213\t    fn bin_of(&self, hash: u64) -> usize {\n214\t        (hash % self.bins.len() as u64) as usize\n215\t    }\n216\t\n217\t    fn alloc_slot(&mut self, hash: u64, key: K, value: V) -> Result<u32, Error> {\n218\t        if let Some(free_idx) = self.free {\n219\t            let next_free = match &self.slots[free_idx as usize].state {\n220\t                SlotState::Free { next_free } => *next_free,\n221\t                SlotState::Filled { .. } => unreachable!(),\n222\t            };\n223\t            let r#gen = self.slots[free_idx as usize].generation;\n224\t            self.slots[free_idx as usize] = Slot {\n225\t                generation: r#gen,\n226\t                state: SlotState::Filled {\n227\t                    hash,\n228\t                    key,\n229\t                    value,\n230\t                    next_in_bin: None,\n231\t                },\n232\t            };\n233\t            self.free = next_free;\n234\t            Ok(free_idx)\n235\t        } else {\n236\t            let idx = self.slots.len();\n237\t            if idx > u32::MAX as usize {\n238\t                return Err(Error::Memory);\n239\t            }\n240\t            self.slots.push(Slot {\n241\t                generation: 0,\n242\t                state: SlotState::Filled {\n243\t                    hash,\n244\t                    key,\n245\t                    value,\n246\t                    next_in_bin: None,\n247\t                },\n248\t            });\n249\t            Ok(idx as u32)\n250\t        }\n251\t    }\n252\t\n253\t    fn release_slot(&mut self, idx: u32) -> (K, V) {\n254\t        let r#gen = self.slots[idx as usize].generation.wrapping_add(1);\n255\t        let old = core::mem::replace(\n256\t            &mut self.slots[idx as usize],\n257\t            Slot {\n258\t                generation: r#gen,\n259\t                state: SlotState::Free {\n260\t                    next_free: self.free,\n261\t                },\n262\t            },\n263\t        );\n264\t        self.free = Some(idx);\n265\t        match old.state {\n266\t            SlotState::Filled { key, value, .. } => (key, value),\n267\t            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n268\t        }\n269\t    }\n270\t\n271\t    fn token_of(&self, idx: u32) -> HashToken {\n272\t        HashToken {\n273\t            idx,\n274\t            generation: self.slots[idx as usize].generation,\n275\t        }\n276\t    }\n277\t\n278\t    fn is_valid(&self, t: HashToken) -> bool {\n279\t        let i = t.idx as usize;\n280\t        i < self.slots.len()\n281\t            && matches!(self.slots[i].state, SlotState::Filled { .. })\n282\t            && self.slots[i].generation == t.generation\n283\t    }\n284\t\n285\t    fn slot_hash(&self, idx: u32) -> u64 {\n286\t        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n287\t            SlotState::Filled { hash, .. } => *hash,\n288\t            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n289\t        }\n290\t    }\n291\t\n292\t    fn slot_key(&self, idx: u32) -> &K {\n293\t        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n294\t            SlotState::Filled { key, .. } => key,\n295\t            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n296\t        }\n297\t    }\n298\t\n299\t    fn slot_value(&self, idx: u32) -> &V {\n300\t        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n301\t            SlotState::Filled { value, .. } => value,\n302\t            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n303\t        }\n304\t    }\n305\t\n306\t    fn slot_value_mut(&mut self, idx: u32) -> &mut V {\n307\t        match &mut self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n308\t            SlotState::Filled { value, .. } => value,\n309\t            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n310\t        }\n311\t    }\n312\t\n313\t    fn slot_next(&self, idx: u32) -> Option<u32> {\n314\t        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n315\t            SlotState::Filled { next_in_bin, .. } => *next_in_bin,\n316\t            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n317\t        }\n318\t    }\n319\t\n320\t    fn set_next(&mut self, idx: u32, next: Option<u32>) {\n321\t        match &mut self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n322\t            SlotState::Filled { next_in_bin, .. } => *next_in_bin = next,\n323\t            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n324\t        }\n325\t    }\n326\t\n327\t    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n328\t    // Public API\n329\t\n330\t    /// Insert `(key, value)` and return a [`HashToken`].\n331\t    /// If `key` was already present, the previous value is replaced.\n332\t    ///\n333\t    /// Returns [`Error::Memory`] on slot-vector allocation failure.\n334\t    pub fn insert(&mut self, key: K, value: V) -> Result<(HashToken, Option<V>), Error> {\n335\t        let hash = self.hash_key(&key);\n336\t        let bin = self.bin_of(hash);\n337\t\n338\t        // Check for existing key.\n339\t        let mut cur = self.bins[bin];\n340\t        while let Some(idx) = cur {\n341\t            if self.slot_key(idx) == &key {\n342\t                let old = core::mem::replace(self.slot_value_mut(idx), value);\n343\t                return Ok((self.token_of(idx), Some(old)));\n344\t            }\n345\t            cur = self.slot_next(idx);\n346\t        }\n347\t\n348\t        // New entry: prepend to bin chain.\n349\t        let idx = self.alloc_slot(hash, key, value)?;\n350\t        let old_head = self.bins[bin];\n351\t        self.set_next(idx, old_head);\n352\t        self.bins[bin] = Some(idx);\n353\t        self.len += 1;\n354\t        Ok((self.token_of(idx), None))\n355\t    }\n356\t\n357\t    /// Look up `key`, returning the matching token or `None`.\n358\t    /// Equivalent to `picohash_retrieve` but typed.\n359\t    pub fn lookup(&self, key: &K) -> Option<HashToken> {\n360\t        let hash = self.hash_key(key);\n361\t        let bin = self.bin_of(hash);\n362\t        let mut cur = self.bins[bin];\n363\t        while let Some(idx) = cur {\n364\t            if self.slot_key(idx) == key {\n365\t                return Some(self.token_of(idx));\n366\t            }\n367\t            cur = self.slot_next(idx);\n368\t        }\n369\t        None\n370\t    }\n371\t\n372\t    /// Borrow the value at `token`, or `None` if the token is stale.\n373\t    pub fn get(&self, token: HashToken) -> Option<&V> {\n374\t        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n375\t            return None;\n376\t        }\n377\t        Some(self.slot_value(token.idx))\n378\t    }\n379\t\n380\t    /// Mutably borrow the value at `token`, or `None` if the token\n381\t    /// is stale.\n382\t    pub fn get_mut(&mut self, token: HashToken) -> Option<&mut V> {\n383\t        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n384\t            return None;\n385\t        }\n386\t        Some(self.slot_value_mut(token.idx))\n387\t    }\n388\t\n389\t    /// Borrow the `(key, value)` pair at `token`.\n390\t    pub fn get_key_value(&self, token: HashToken) -> Option<(&K, &V)> {\n391\t        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n392\t            return None;\n393\t        }\n394\t        Some((self.slot_key(token.idx), self.slot_value(token.idx)))\n395\t    }\n396\t\n397\t    /// Remove and return the entry at `token`.  Bumps the slot's\n398\t    /// generation.  Returns `None` if the token was already stale.\n399\t    pub fn remove(&mut self, token: HashToken) -> Option<(K, V)> {\n400\t        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n401\t            return None;\n402\t        }\n403\t        let idx = token.idx;\n404\t        let hash = self.slot_hash(idx);\n405\t        let bin = self.bin_of(hash);\n406\t\n407\t        // Unlink from bin chain.\n408\t        let head = self.bins[bin];\n409\t        if head == Some(idx) {\n410\t            let next = self.slot_next(idx);\n411\t            self.bins[bin] = next;\n412\t        } else {\n413\t            let mut prev = head.unwrap();\n414\t            loop {\n415\t                let next = self.slot_next(prev);\n416\t                if next == Some(idx) {\n417\t                    let after = self.slot_next(idx);\n418\t                    self.set_next(prev, after);\n419\t                    break;\n420\t                }\n421\t                prev = next.unwrap();\n422\t            }\n423\t        }\n424\t\n425\t        self.len -= 1;\n426\t        Some(self.release_slot(idx))\n427\t    }\n428\t\n429\t    /// Remove the entry matching `key`.  Prefer [`HashTable::remove`]\n430\t    /// when a token is on hand.\n431\t    pub fn remove_by_key(&mut self, key: &K) -> Option<V> {\n432\t        let tok = self.lookup(key)?;\n433\t        self.remove(tok).map(|(_, v)| v)\n434\t    }\n435\t\n436\t    /// `true` if `key` is currently in the table.\n437\t    pub fn contains_key(&self, key: &K) -> bool {\n438\t        self.lookup(key).is_some()\n439\t    }\n440\t\n441\t    /// Number of live entries.\n442\t    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {\n443\t        self.len\n444\t    }\n445\t\n446\t    /// `true` when `len() == 0`.\n447\t    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {\n448\t        self.len() == 0\n449\t    }\n450\t\n451\t    /// Drop every entry.  Tokens issued before the call are stale\n452\t    /// after it.\n453\t    pub fn clear(&mut self) {\n454\t        self.slots.clear();\n455\t        self.free = None;\n456\t        for b in &mut self.bins {\n457\t            *b = None;\n458\t        }\n459\t        self.len = 0;\n460\t    }\n461\t}\n462\t\n463\t/// picoquic's bespoke byte-string hash, used by\n464\t/// `connection_id_hash` for short connection IDs where SipHash\n465\t/// would be overkill.  Kept as a free function (rather than a\n466\t/// `Hasher` impl) for source-level parity with the C body.\n467\t///\n468\t/// C: `picohash_bytes`.\n469\tpub fn hash_bytes(bytes: &[u8], hash_seed: &[u8; 16]) -> u64 {\n470\t    let mut hash = u64::from_le_bytes(hash_seed[8..16].try_into().unwrap());\n471\t    let mut rotate: u32 = 11;\n472\t    for (i, &b) in bytes.iter().enumerate() {\n473\t        hash ^= b as u64;\n474\t        hash ^= hash_seed[i & 15] as u64;\n475\t        hash ^= hash << 8;\n476\t        hash = hash.wrapping_add(hash >> rotate);\n477\t        rotate = (hash & 31) as u32 + 11;\n478\t    }\n479\t    hash ^= hash >> rotate;\n480\t    hash\n481\t}\n482\t\n483\t#[cfg(test)]\n484\tmod test {}\n485\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6df50c8-84e7-456d-b33a-aec683aa6926","uuid":"69357735-0724-4703-b226-af1f36e85c0c","timestamp":"2026-05-05T17:01:39.037Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/hash.rs","content":"//! Token-based hash table.\n//!\n//! Replaces the C `picohash_table` (an open-addressed table with\n//! chained collision lists, intrusive `picohash_item`s embedded in\n//! the caller's structs and a function-pointer trio for hashing /\n//! comparing / projecting the embedded item).\n//!\n//! ## API shape\n//!\n//! `HashTable<K, V>` is a slotmap-backed hash map.  `K: Hash + Eq`\n//! provides the key contract; `V` is whatever the caller stores\n//! (usually a token into some other arena — see Phase-4 plan\n//! below).  The trio of C function pointers is gone: hashing comes\n//! from `K`'s `Hash` impl, comparison from `Eq`, and the table\n//! never reaches into the caller's struct so no `key_to_item`\n//! callback is needed.\n//!\n//! Operations return [`HashToken`]s — opaque (`idx, generation`)\n//! handles into this table's slot vector.  Tokens are `Copy`,\n//! survive insertion and removal of *other* keys, but become stale\n//! the moment the keyed entry is removed (the slot's generation\n//! bumps).  [`HashTable::get`] returns `None` for stale tokens —\n//! the safe equivalent of the C dangling-`HashItem*` use-after-free.\n//!\n//! ## Phase 4 plan — implementation\n//!\n//! The bodies in this module are `todo!()`.  Phase 4 picks one of:\n//!\n//! 1. **Hand-roll the slotmap.**  Internal layout (illustrative):\n//!\n//!    ```ignore\n//!    struct Slot<K, V> {\n//!        generation: u32,\n//!        state: SlotState<K, V>,\n//!    }\n//!    enum SlotState<K, V> {\n//!        Free   { next_free: Option<u32> },\n//!        Filled { hash: u64, key: K, value: V, next_in_bin: Option<u32> },\n//!    }\n//!    pub struct HashTable<K, V> {\n//!        slots: Vec<Slot<K, V>>,\n//!        free:  Option<u32>,\n//!        bins:  Vec<Option<u32>>,\n//!        seed:  [u8; 16],\n//!        len:   usize,\n//!    }\n//!    ```\n//!\n//!    `next_in_bin` lives inside the slot, not the user struct, so\n//!    no `unsafe`.  Lookup hashes `K` to a bin index, walks the\n//!    chain by following `next_in_bin` slot indices, comparing each\n//!    `slot.key` against the target.  Insert pushes a new slot\n//!    (or pops one off the free list) and threads it onto the bin\n//!    chain.  Remove unlinks, marks the slot `Free`, bumps\n//!    generation, and adds it to the free list.\n//!\n//! 2. **Build on the `slotmap` crate.**  `slotmap::SlotMap` already\n//!    provides the slot/generation/free-list machinery; this module\n//!    layers the bin-array indexing on top.  The crate is\n//!    `no_std`-friendly with the right features and would let us\n//!    delete maybe 80% of the implementation.\n//!\n//! Either implementation should keep `HashToken` byte-compatible\n//! with the public API below — the choice is local.\n//!\n//! ## Phase 4 plan — call sites\n//!\n//! In the C tree, every hash table is intrusive: the value type\n//! embeds a `HashItem` field and the table's bins point straight\n//! into the middle of those user-owned objects.  In the Rust port\n//! the embedding turns into a *membership token*: the parent\n//! struct holds `Option<HashToken>` for each table it can be in,\n//! and the table's slot stores the parent's `ConnectionToken`\n//! (or other token type) into the arena that owns the parent.\n//!\n//! For example, `quic.connection_by_id: HashTable<ConnectionId,\n//! ConnectionToken>` points at connections that live in\n//! `quic.connections: Arena<Connection>`.  A `Connection` carries\n//! `connection_by_id_membership: Option<HashToken>`; on removal the\n//! Connection hands that token back for an O(1) `connection_by_id.remove`.\n\nextern crate alloc;\nuse alloc::vec::Vec;\n\nuse core::hash::{Hash, Hasher};\n\nuse crate::Error;\n\n/// Opaque handle into a [`HashTable`]'s slot vector.\n///\n/// `idx` selects a slot; `generation` is incremented on every\n/// removal so an old token comparing against a recycled slot\n/// returns `None` from [`HashTable::get`].  The pair is `Copy` and\n/// 64-bit total — call sites pass it by value.\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]\npub struct HashToken {\n    idx: u32,\n    generation: u32,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Internal slot storage\n\nstruct Slot<K, V> {\n    generation: u32,\n    state: SlotState<K, V>,\n}\n\nenum SlotState<K, V> {\n    Free {\n        next_free: Option<u32>,\n    },\n    Filled {\n        hash: u64,\n        key: K,\n        value: V,\n        next_in_bin: Option<u32>,\n    },\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Seeded hasher — streams bytes through the picohash_bytes mixing function.\n\nstruct SeedHasher {\n    hash: u64,\n    rotate: u32,\n    seed: [u8; 16],\n    byte_idx: u32,\n}\n\nimpl SeedHasher {\n    fn new(seed: &[u8; 16]) -> Self {\n        let hash = u64::from_le_bytes(seed[8..16].try_into().unwrap());\n        SeedHasher {\n            hash,\n            rotate: 11,\n            seed: *seed,\n            byte_idx: 0,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Hasher for SeedHasher {\n    fn write(&mut self, bytes: &[u8]) {\n        for &b in bytes {\n            self.hash ^= b as u64;\n            self.hash ^= self.seed[(self.byte_idx & 15) as usize] as u64;\n            self.hash ^= self.hash << 8;\n            self.hash = self.hash.wrapping_add(self.hash >> self.rotate);\n            self.rotate = (self.hash & 31) as u32 + 11;\n            self.byte_idx = self.byte_idx.wrapping_add(1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn finish(&self) -> u64 {\n        let mut h = self.hash;\n        h ^= h >> self.rotate;\n        h\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n/// Hash table mapping `K` to `V`, addressable by [`HashToken`].\n///\n/// The value `V` is typically a token into some other arena (see\n/// the Phase-4 call-site plan in the module docs) but any owned\n/// value works.  `K: Hash + Eq` is the only contract on the key.\npub struct HashTable<K, V> {\n    slots: Vec<Slot<K, V>>,\n    free: Option<u32>,\n    bins: Vec<Option<u32>>,\n    seed: [u8; 16],\n    len: usize,\n}\n\nimpl<K: Hash + Eq, V> HashTable<K, V> {\n    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Constructors\n\n    /// Build an empty table with `nb_bin` collision bins, using a\n    /// zero hash seed.\n    ///\n    /// C: `picohash_create`.\n    pub fn new(nb_bin: usize) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n        Self::with_seed(nb_bin, &[0u8; 16])\n    }\n\n    /// Like [`HashTable::new`] but with a caller-supplied 16-byte\n    /// hash seed.\n    ///\n    /// C: `picohash_create_ex`.\n    pub fn with_seed(nb_bin: usize, hash_seed: &[u8; 16]) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n        let bins = alloc::vec![None; nb_bin];\n        Ok(Self {\n            slots: Vec::new(),\n            free: None,\n            bins,\n            seed: *hash_seed,\n            len: 0,\n        })\n    }\n\n    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Internal helpers\n\n    fn hash_key(&self, key: &K) -> u64 {\n        let mut h = SeedHasher::new(&self.seed);\n        key.hash(&mut h);\n        h.finish()\n    }\n\n    fn bin_of(&self, hash: u64) -> usize {\n        (hash % self.bins.len() as u64) as usize\n    }\n\n    fn alloc_slot(&mut self, hash: u64, key: K, value: V) -> Result<u32, Error> {\n        if let Some(free_idx) = self.free {\n            let next_free = match &self.slots[free_idx as usize].state {\n                SlotState::Free { next_free } => *next_free,\n                SlotState::Filled { .. } => unreachable!(),\n            };\n            let r#gen = self.slots[free_idx as usize].generation;\n            self.slots[free_idx as usize] = Slot {\n                generation: r#gen,\n                state: SlotState::Filled {\n                    hash,\n                    key,\n                    value,\n                    next_in_bin: None,\n                },\n            };\n            self.free = next_free;\n            Ok(free_idx)\n        } else {\n            let idx = self.slots.len();\n            if idx > u32::MAX as usize {\n                return Err(Error::Memory);\n            }\n            self.slots.push(Slot {\n                generation: 0,\n                state: SlotState::Filled {\n                    hash,\n                    key,\n                    value,\n                    next_in_bin: None,\n                },\n            });\n            Ok(idx as u32)\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn release_slot(&mut self, idx: u32) -> (K, V) {\n        let r#gen = self.slots[idx as usize].generation.wrapping_add(1);\n        let old = core::mem::replace(\n            &mut self.slots[idx as usize],\n            Slot {\n                generation: r#gen,\n                state: SlotState::Free {\n                    next_free: self.free,\n                },\n            },\n        );\n        self.free = Some(idx);\n        match old.state {\n            SlotState::Filled { key, value, .. } => (key, value),\n            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn token_of(&self, idx: u32) -> HashToken {\n        HashToken {\n            idx,\n            generation: self.slots[idx as usize].generation,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn is_valid(&self, t: HashToken) -> bool {\n        let i = t.idx as usize;\n        i < self.slots.len()\n            && matches!(self.slots[i].state, SlotState::Filled { .. })\n            && self.slots[i].generation == t.generation\n    }\n\n    fn slot_hash(&self, idx: u32) -> u64 {\n        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n            SlotState::Filled { hash, .. } => *hash,\n            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn slot_key(&self, idx: u32) -> &K {\n        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n            SlotState::Filled { key, .. } => key,\n            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn slot_value(&self, idx: u32) -> &V {\n        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n            SlotState::Filled { value, .. } => value,\n            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn slot_value_mut(&mut self, idx: u32) -> &mut V {\n        match &mut self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n            SlotState::Filled { value, .. } => value,\n            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn slot_next(&self, idx: u32) -> Option<u32> {\n        match &self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n            SlotState::Filled { next_in_bin, .. } => *next_in_bin,\n            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn set_next(&mut self, idx: u32, next: Option<u32>) {\n        match &mut self.slots[idx as usize].state {\n            SlotState::Filled { next_in_bin, .. } => *next_in_bin = next,\n            SlotState::Free { .. } => unreachable!(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Public API\n\n    /// Insert `(key, value)` and return a [`HashToken`].\n    /// If `key` was already present, the previous value is replaced.\n    ///\n    /// Returns [`Error::Memory`] on slot-vector allocation failure.\n    pub fn insert(&mut self, key: K, value: V) -> Result<(HashToken, Option<V>), Error> {\n        let hash = self.hash_key(&key);\n        let bin = self.bin_of(hash);\n\n        // Check for existing key.\n        let mut cur = self.bins[bin];\n        while let Some(idx) = cur {\n            if self.slot_key(idx) == &key {\n                let old = core::mem::replace(self.slot_value_mut(idx), value);\n                return Ok((self.token_of(idx), Some(old)));\n            }\n            cur = self.slot_next(idx);\n        }\n\n        // New entry: prepend to bin chain.\n        let idx = self.alloc_slot(hash, key, value)?;\n        let old_head = self.bins[bin];\n        self.set_next(idx, old_head);\n        self.bins[bin] = Some(idx);\n        self.len += 1;\n        Ok((self.token_of(idx), None))\n    }\n\n    /// Look up `key`, returning the matching token or `None`.\n    /// Equivalent to `picohash_retrieve` but typed.\n    pub fn lookup(&self, key: &K) -> Option<HashToken> {\n        let hash = self.hash_key(key);\n        let bin = self.bin_of(hash);\n        let mut cur = self.bins[bin];\n        while let Some(idx) = cur {\n            if self.slot_key(idx) == key {\n                return Some(self.token_of(idx));\n            }\n            cur = self.slot_next(idx);\n        }\n        None\n    }\n\n    /// Borrow the value at `token`, or `None` if the token is stale.\n    pub fn get(&self, token: HashToken) -> Option<&V> {\n        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n            return None;\n        }\n        Some(self.slot_value(token.idx))\n    }\n\n    /// Mutably borrow the value at `token`, or `None` if the token\n    /// is stale.\n    pub fn get_mut(&mut self, token: HashToken) -> Option<&mut V> {\n        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n            return None;\n        }\n        Some(self.slot_value_mut(token.idx))\n    }\n\n    /// Borrow the `(key, value)` pair at `token`.\n    pub fn get_key_value(&self, token: HashToken) -> Option<(&K, &V)> {\n        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n            return None;\n        }\n        Some((self.slot_key(token.idx), self.slot_value(token.idx)))\n    }\n\n    /// Remove and return the entry at `token`.  Bumps the slot's\n    /// generation.  Returns `None` if the token was already stale.\n    pub fn remove(&mut self, token: HashToken) -> Option<(K, V)> {\n        if !self.is_valid(token) {\n            return None;\n        }\n        let idx = token.idx;\n        let hash = self.slot_hash(idx);\n        let bin = self.bin_of(hash);\n\n        // Unlink from bin chain.\n        let head = self.bins[bin];\n        if head == Some(idx) {\n            let next = self.slot_next(idx);\n            self.bins[bin] = next;\n        } else {\n            let mut prev = head.unwrap();\n            loop {\n                let next = self.slot_next(prev);\n                if next == Some(idx) {\n                    let after = self.slot_next(idx);\n                    self.set_next(prev, after);\n                    break;\n                }\n                prev = next.unwrap();\n            }\n        }\n\n        self.len -= 1;\n        Some(self.release_slot(idx))\n    }\n\n    /// Remove the entry matching `key`.  Prefer [`HashTable::remove`]\n    /// when a token is on hand.\n    pub fn remove_by_key(&mut self, key: &K) -> Option<V> {\n        let tok = self.lookup(key)?;\n        self.remove(tok).map(|(_, v)| v)\n    }\n\n    /// `true` if `key` is currently in the table.\n    pub fn contains_key(&self, key: &K) -> bool {\n        self.lookup(key).is_some()\n    }\n\n    /// Number of live entries.\n    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {\n        self.len\n    }\n\n    /// `true` when `len() == 0`.\n    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {\n        self.len() == 0\n    }\n\n    /// Drop every entry.  Tokens issued before the call are stale\n    /// after it.\n    pub fn clear(&mut self) {\n        self.slots.clear();\n        self.free = None;\n        for b in &mut self.bins {\n            *b = None;\n        }\n        self.len = 0;\n    }\n}\n\n/// picoquic's bespoke byte-string hash, used by\n/// `connection_id_hash` for short connection IDs where SipHash\n/// would be overkill.  Kept as a free function (rather than a\n/// `Hasher` impl) for source-level parity with the C body.\n///\n/// C: `picohash_bytes`.\npub fn hash_bytes(bytes: &[u8], hash_seed: &[u8; 16]) -> u64 {\n    let mut hash = u64::from_le_bytes(hash_seed[8..16].try_into().unwrap());\n    let mut rotate: u32 = 11;\n    for (i, &b) in bytes.iter().enumerate() {\n        hash ^= b as u64;\n        hash ^= hash_seed[i & 15] as u64;\n        hash ^= hash << 8;\n        hash = hash.wrapping_add(hash >> rotate);\n        rotate = (hash & 31) as u32 + 11;\n    }\n    hash ^= hash >> rotate;\n    hash\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod test {}\n","numLines":485,"startLine":1,"totalLines":485}}}
