{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZMJG4GaKZNU5XawepyoKT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Numeric error codes used over the QUIC wire and inside picoquic.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Two distinct ranges:\n4\t//!\n5\t//! * [`InternalError`] — picoquic-private codes allocated in the\n6\t//!   `0x400`+ range so they never collide with QUIC transport or\n7\t//!   TLS alert codes.  Surface inside the library; never put on the\n8\t//!   wire.\n9\t//! * [`TransportError`] — QUIC transport / TLS-alert codes from\n10\t//!   RFC 9000 §20 (and various drafts).  These cross the wire in\n11\t//!   CONNECTION_CLOSE frames.\n12\t//!\n13\t//! The `crate::Error` enum (defined in `lib.rs`) is the richer Rust\n14\t//! error surface used by fallible APIs; these enums provide the\n15\t//! numeric on-wire / on-log codes those errors map to.\n16\t\n17\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18\t// Picoquic-internal errors.\n19\t\n20\t/// Base offset for picoquic's internal error codes.  Allocated in\n21\t/// the `0x400`+ range so they never collide with QUIC transport or\n22\t/// TLS alert codes.\n23\tpub const ERROR_CLASS: u64 = 0x400;\n24\t\n25\t/// Picoquic-internal error code.  Numeric values follow C source.\n26\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n27\t#[repr(u64)]\n28\tpub enum InternalError {\n29\t    Duplicate = ERROR_CLASS + 1,\n30\t    AeadCheck = ERROR_CLASS + 3,\n31\t    UnexpectedPacket = ERROR_CLASS + 4,\n32\t    Memory = ERROR_CLASS + 5,\n33\t    CnxidCheck = ERROR_CLASS + 7,\n34\t    InitialTooShort = ERROR_CLASS + 8,\n35\t    VersionNegotiationSpoofed = ERROR_CLASS + 9,\n36\t    MalformedTransportExtension = ERROR_CLASS + 10,\n37\t    ExtensionBufferTooSmall = ERROR_CLASS + 11,\n38\t    IllegalTransportExtension = ERROR_CLASS + 12,\n39\t    CannotResetStreamZero = ERROR_CLASS + 13,\n40\t    InvalidStreamId = ERROR_CLASS + 14,\n41\t    StreamAlreadyClosed = ERROR_CLASS + 15,\n42\t    Fra