{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a Phase 4 batch translation task: fill in `todo!()` function bodies in 5 Rust files by translating matching C bodies from `picoquic/`. Total 116 `todo!()` bodies across:\n   - `rs/fq/src/hash.rs` (1 — in doc comment only, already fully implemented)\n   - `rs/fq/src/splay.rs` (1 — in doc comment only, already fully implemented)\n   - `rs/fq/src/utils.rs` (56 bodies, primary focus so far)\n   - `rs/fq/src/tls_api.rs` (42 bodies, not yet started)\n   - `rs/fq/src/packet_loop.rs` (16 bodies, not yet started)\n\n   Rules: faithful + idiomatic translation, no `unsafe`, no signature changes, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/`. After each file run `python3 scripts/phase4_check.py <file>`. Final gate: `cargo fmt`, `cargo test --no-run`, `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - C-to-Rust translation of picoquic QUIC library\n   - Phase 4: filling function bodies (Phase 1/2 designed signatures, Phase 3 wrote tests)\n   - Token-based splay tree and hash table (already complete in hash.rs and splay.rs)\n   - Thread-local storage for debug state (`RefCell<Option<Box<dyn Write>>>`, `Cell<bool>`) to avoid `Send` constraints in single-threaded library\n   - `static Mutex<Option<&'static str>>` + `Box::leak` for solution_dir global\n   - Rust child modules can access private fields of parent module structs (utils.rs is child of lib.rs crate root, so can construct `ConnectionId { id: ..., id_len: ... }` directly)\n   - `SocketAddr::V4`/`V6` replaces C `AF_INET`/`AF_INET6`; `IpAddr::octets()` returns by value (not borrowable as `&[u8]`), hence `get_ip_addr` returns `None`\n   - QUIC varint encoding (RFC 9000 §16): 2-bit tag in high bits determines 1/2/4/8