     - `debug_printf`: checks suspended, writes to DEBUG_OUT\n     - `debug_printf_push_stream`: asserts no existing stream, sets it\n     - `debug_printf_pop_stream`: asserts existing stream, clears it\n     - `debug_printf_suspend/resume/reset`: Cell set/get operations\n     - `debug_dump`: 16-byte hex chunks to DEBUG_OUT\n     - `sprintf`: copy to buf with NUL terminator, Err on truncation\n     - `format_connection_id`: copy id bytes to output slice\n     - `parse_connection_id`: copy bytes to ConnectionId struct (private fields accessible from child module)\n     - `hash_addr_bytes`: copy IP octets + port (native endian) to bytes buffer\n     - `hash_addr`: calls `hash_addr_bytes` then `crate::siphash::siphash`\n     - `parse_hexa`: with nested `hexa_digit` helper function\n     - `parse_connection_id_hexa`: calls `parse_hexa` with 18-byte limit (matching C)\n     - `print_connection_id_hexa`: write each byte as `{:02x}`\n     - `compare_addr`: IP compare + port compare\n     - `compare_ip_addr`: match on V4/V6 variants, octets().cmp()\n     - `get_addr_port`: `addr.port()`\n     - `set_addr_port`: `addr.set_port(port)`\n     - `addr_length`: 16 (V4) or 28 (V6)\n     - `store_addr`: `addr.copied()`\n     - `get_ip_addr`: returns `None` (cannot safely borrow IP bytes from SocketAddr)\n     - `store_text_addr`: `ip_address_text.parse::<IpAddr>()`\n     - `addr_text`: `write!(w, \"{}:{}\", ...)` or `\"[{}]:{}\"` for V6\n     - `store_loopback_addr`: cfg-based AF_INET6 constant, calls store_text_addr\n     - `set_preferred_address`: parses v4/v6 text, validates family, stores in PreferredAddress.v4/.v6\n     \n     Still pending (not yet edited in utils.rs):\n     - `set_solution_dir`, `solution_dir`, `get_input_path`\n     - `file_delete`\n     - All `frames_*` functions (fixed_skip, varint_skip, varint_decode, varlen_decode, uint8/16/32/64_decode, length_data_skip, cid_decode, varint_encode_length, varint_encode, varlen_encode, uint8/16/24/32/64_encode, length_data_encode, cid_encode, charz_encode)\n     - `constant_time_memcmp`\n     - `uint8_to_str`\n\n   - **`picoquic/util.c`** — C source (1439 lines) containing all utility implementations. Read in full for translation reference.\n   \n   - **`rs/fq/src/lib.rs`** — Crate root. Defines `ConnectionId` with private fields (`id: [u8; 20]`, `id_len: u8`), `Error` enum, `CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE = 20`. ConnectionId also has `todo!()` methods `clone_from_slice`, `with_size`, `hash_with_seed`, `val64` — but these are NOT in the batch, and the child-module field access means utils.rs doesn't need them.\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tp.rs`** — Defines `PreferredAddress`:\n     ```rust\n     pub struct PreferredAddress {\n         pub v4: Option<SocketAddr>,\n         pub v6: Option<SocketAddr>,\n         pub connection_id: ConnectionId,\n         pub stateless_reset_token: [u8; 16],\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tls_api.rs`** — Read but not yet edited. 42 todo!() bodies covering: master TLS context init/free, per-connection TLS context, TLS stream processing, initial secret derivation, AEAD contexts, retry tokens, AES-128-ECB context, hash creation, cert loading, etc. Source: `picoquic/tls_api.c` (3218 lines).\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/packet_loop.rs`** — Read but not yet edited. 16 todo!() bodies covering: `Quic::run_v2`, `Quic::run`, `NetworkThreadCtx::run/spawn/spawn_custom/wake_up`, `internal_thread_create/delete/setname`, `Quic::thread_ctx`, `Quic::create_server`, `Config::start_server_threads`, `SocketCtx::close`, `open_sockets`. Source: `picoquic/sockloop.c` (2065 lines). Many threading functions are \"out of v1 scope\" per TRANSLATE_PLAN.md.\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/errors.rs`** — Read to understand Error variants. `InternalError` enum with numeric codes; the public `Error` enum in lib.rs has: `Generic, Memory, InvalidArgument, BufferTooSmall, NoSuchFile, InvalidFile, Disconnected, InvalidState, InvalidFrame, Tls, Protocol(u64)`.\n\n   - **`rs/fq/Cargo.toml`** — Dependencies: `fugit`