{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y1kdNRQcs4VgJ2kE1xwppm","type":"tool_result","content":"884\t## Phase 4 — Translate implementations\n885\t\n886\tAfter Phase 3 lands, every public test is expressed as Rust against the\n887\tdesigned API surface, and the body of every API method is `todo!()`.\n888\tPhase 4 fills those bodies by translating the matching C body from\n889\t`picoquic/<src>.c`.  The Phase 3 test suite is the gate: a function is\n890\t\"done\" when the tests that exercise it stop panicking on `todo!()`.\n891\t\n892\t### Order (default: file size; opt-in: call-graph height)\n893\t\n894\tTargets are the `.rs` files under `rs/fq/src/` that still contain\n895\t`todo!()` bodies (test files, sys/loglib stubs, and out-of-v1-scope\n896\tmodules are skipped — see `SKIP_FILES` in `scripts/phase4.py`).\n897\t\n898\tDefault ordering is by file size (smallest first) — a crude but\n899\teffective leaf-first proxy.  Leaf modules (`siphash`, `splay`, `hash`,\n900\t`bytestream`) are short; `Connection` / `Quic` core in `internal.rs` is\n901\thuge.\n902\t\n903\tOpt-in ordering with `--order callgraph` reads `xlate/call_graph.json`\n904\t(`height_of`) and sorts by the *minimum* C call-graph height of any\n905\tfunction whose name appears in `/// C: \\`name\\`` doc comments inside the\n906\tfile.  Files with no matched names fall through to size order.  Use\n907\tthis when the size proxy gets fooled by a big file full of\n908\tindependent leaves (e.g. `utils.rs`).\n909\t\n910\t### Pipeline (`scripts/phase4.py`)\n911\t\n912\tFor each Rust source file:\n913\t\n914\t1. **Compose a prompt** that:\n915\t   * names the Rust target and its `todo!()` count;\n916\t   * points at `xlate/impl_translation_guide.md` for C → Rust idiom\n917\t     mappings (memory, control flow, errors, strings, time, network,\n918\t     logging, crypto);\n919\t   * names the matching C source(s) — the doc comments in the Rust\n920\t     file already encode this as `/// C: \\`picoquic_xxx\\``;\n921\t   * spells out the translation contract (faithful, idiomatic, no\n922\t     signature changes, no `unsafe`, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/`).\n923\t2. **Invoke `claude -p`** with a tight allowlist (Read / Edit /\n924\t   Glob / Grep / Bash for `cargo` and the Phase 4 completion check).\n925\t3. **Verify** with `scripts/phase4_check.py <rs file>` (zero\n926\t   `todo!()`s remain in the named files).\n927\t4. **Build gate** — `cargo fmt` + `cargo test --no-run` + `cargo\n928\t   clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.  Failure penalises\n929\t   the run.\n930\t\n931\tA `--batch N` mode packs N source files per claude invocation,\n932\tamortising the guide read and any cross-module API lookups.  The\n933\tbuild gate runs once at the end of each batch.\n934\t\n935\tState / log artifacts:\n936\t\n937\t* `xlate/phase4_state.json` — per-file `{status, at, …}`.  `ok` /\n938\t  `partial` / `fail`; `partial` records `remaining` count.\n939\t* `xlate/phase4_runs/<timestamp>.log` — per-sweep tee of stdout.\n940\t* `xlate/claude_logs/phase4/<basename>.log` — per-run stream-json\n941\t  transcript of the claude invocation.\n942\t* `xlate/prompts/phase4/<basename>.md` — the composed prompt\n943\t  (regenerated on each run).\n944\t\n945\tRe-running with no flags resumes from `phase4_state.json` (already-`ok`\n946\tfiles are skipped).  `--force` redoes everything; `--src <file>`\n947\ttargets one file; `--limit N` caps the sweep.  HTTP 429 is detected\n948\t(both `api_error_status==429` *and* `is_error`) and aborts cleanly\n949\twithout polluting state.\n950\t\n951\t### Signature drift\n952\t\n953\tWhen translating function `f`, the translator may discover that the\n954\tPhase 1 signature for some callee `g` is wrong.  Surface it on\n955\tstdout and stop — that's a human design call, not Phase 4 work.\n956\tPhase 1 / 2 / 3 settled the surface; Phase 4 only fills bodies.\n957\t\n958\t### Discovered call edges\n959\t\n960\tStatic analysis under-approximates call edges through function\n961\tpointers and trait objects.  When `cargo test` reveals a `todo!()`\n962\tpanic in a function the call graph thought was a leaf, the\n963\ttranslator implements the required trait method and moves on — no"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6df50c8-84e7-456d-b33a-aec683aa6926","uuid":"f2b73802-995f-41e5-84dc-d86be67c223e","timestamp":"2026-05-05T17:23:22.414Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/TRANSLATE_PLAN.md","content":"## Phase 4 — Translate implementations\n\nAfter Phase 3 lands, every public test is expressed as Rust against the\ndesigned API surface, and the body of every API method is `todo!()`.\nPhase 4 fills those bodies by translating the matching C body from\n`picoquic/<src>.c`.  The Phase 3 test suite is the gate: a function is\n\"done\" when the tests that exercise it stop panicking on `todo!()`.\n\n### Order (default: file size; opt-in: call-graph height)\n\nTargets are the `.rs` files under `rs/fq/src/` that still contain\n`todo!()` bodies (test files, sys/loglib stubs, and out-of-v1-scope\nmodules are skipped — see `SKIP_FILES` in `scripts/phase4.py`).\n\nDefault ordering is by file size (smallest first) — a crude but\neffective leaf-first proxy.  Leaf modules (`siphash`, `splay`, `hash`,\n`bytestream`) are short; `Connection` / `Quic` core in `internal.rs` is\nhuge.\n\nOpt-in ordering with `--order callgraph` reads `xlate/call_graph.json`\n(`height_of`) and sorts by the *minimum* C call-graph height of any\nfunction whose name appears in `/// C: \\`name\\`` doc comments inside the\nfile.  Files with no matched names fall through to size order.  Use\nthis when the size proxy gets fooled by a big file full of\nindependent leaves (e.g. `utils.rs`).\n\n### Pipeline (`scripts/phase4.py`)\n\nFor each Rust source file:\n\n1. **Compose a prompt** that:\n   * names the Rust target and its `todo!()` count;\n   * points at `xlate/impl_translation_guide.md` for C → Rust idiom\n     mappings (memory, control flow, errors, strings, time, network,\n     logging, crypto);\n   * names the matching C source(s) — the doc comments in the Rust\n     file already encode this as `/// C: \\`picoquic_xxx\\``;\n   * spells out the translation contract (faithful, idiomatic, no\n     signature changes, no `unsafe`, no edits outside `rs/fq/src/`).\n2. **Invoke `claude -p`** with a tight allowlist (Read / Edit /\n   Glob / Grep / Bash for `cargo` and the Phase 4 completion check).\n3. **Verify** with `scripts/phase4_check.py <rs file>` (zero\n   `todo!()`s remain in the named files).\n4. **Build gate** — `cargo fmt` + `cargo test --no-run` + `cargo\n   clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.  Failure penalises\n   the run.\n\nA `--batch N` mode packs N source files per claude invocation,\namortising the guide read and any cross-module API lookups.  The\nbuild gate runs once at the end of each batch.\n\nState / log artifacts:\n\n* `xlate/phase4_state.json` — per-file `{status, at, …}`.  `ok` /\n  `partial` / `fail`; `partial` records `remaining` count.\n* `xlate/phase4_runs/<timestamp>.log` — per-sweep tee of stdout.\n* `xlate/claude_logs/phase4/<basename>.log` — per-run stream-json\n  transcript of the claude invocation.\n* `xlate/prompts/phase4/<basename>.md` — the composed prompt\n  (regenerated on each run).\n\nRe-running with no flags resumes from `phase4_state.json` (already-`ok`\nfiles are skipped).  `--force` redoes everything; `--src <file>`\ntargets one file; `--limit N` caps the sweep.  HTTP 429 is detected\n(both `api_error_status==429` *and* `is_error`) and aborts cleanly\nwithout polluting state.\n\n### Signature drift\n\nWhen translating function `f`, the translator may discover that the\nPhase 1 signature for some callee `g` is wrong.  Surface it on\nstdout and stop — that's a human design call, not Phase 4 work.\nPhase 1 / 2 / 3 settled the surface; Phase 4 only fills bodies.\n\n### Discovered call edges\n\nStatic analysis under-approximates call edges through function\npointers and trait objects.  When `cargo test` reveals a `todo!()`\npanic in a function the call graph thought was a leaf, the\ntranslator implements the required trait method and moves on — no","numLines":80,"startLine":884,"totalLines":1038}}}
