{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QnteGvMKG22BDmwrPfsN9j","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/internal.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! quic-core's grand internal header.  Anything that is not\n4\t//! part of the published `quic.h` API but is shared between\n5\t//! `.c` files of the core library lives here: connection /\n6\t//! path / stream / packet structures, frame and packet-type\n7\t//! enums, the giant `Quic` and `Connection`\n8\t//! structures that pin the rest of the library together, and\n9\t//! the long internal-only function surface (~200 functions).\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every function body is\n12\t//! `todo!()`.  Test module at the end is intentionally empty;\n13\t//! Phase 2 fills it.\n14\t//!\n15\t//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n16\t//!\n17\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields collapse to\n18\t//!   `bool` per field (the \"ordinary integer field with\n19\t//!   mask/shift accessors\" rule, simplified for the trivial\n20\t//!   1-bit case where `bool` is clearer than `u32` + masks).\n21\t//! * Phase 1B replaced the C intrusive linked-list / splay /\n22\t//!   hash linkage with arena tokens\n23\t//!   ([`crate::arena::Token`], [`crate::splay::SplayToken`],\n24\t//!   [`crate::hash::HashToken`]).  Every per-collection\n25\t//!   membership is `Option<Token>` on the parent struct; the\n26\t//!   container holds the slot storage.  Zero raw pointers, no\n27\t//!   `unsafe`.\n28\t//! * The C `void* tls_master_ctx`, `void* aead_*`,\n29\t//!   `void* pn_enc/dec`, etc. were external-library handles\n30\t//!   ((picotls, OpenSSL).  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n31\t//!   trait family in [`crate::tls`] (`Session`, `PacketKey`,\n32\t//!   `HeaderKey`, …); backends supply implementations.\n33\t//! * `FILE* F_log` / `FILE* f_binlog` became\n34\t//!   `Option<std::fs::File>` in Phase 1B.\n35\t//! * `struct sockaddr_storage` fields fold into\n36\t//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  Fields that the C code zeros out\n37\t//!   to mean \"address not yet set\" become `Option<SocketAddr>`.\n38\t//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` were\n39\t//!   forward-declared as opaque stubs in\n40\t//!   [`crate`] (the public header).  Their\n41\t//!   real bodies live here; the public module re-exports the\n42\t//!   names so existing `use` paths in other modules keep\n43\t//!   working.\n44\t//! * Function pointer typedefs (`autoqlog_fn`,\n45\t//!   `performance_log_fn`, the spin-bit pair, the\n46\t//!   memlog hook on a connection, `mask_fns_t`) collapse to\n47\t//!   traits per the project rule.  When two function pointers\n48\t//!   are always installed together (`SpinbitDef`,\n49\t//!   `mask_fns_t`) they share one trait.\n50\t//! * Conditional fields gated by `BBRExperiment` and\n51\t//!   `WITH_THREAD_CHECK` are dropped — they are not\n52\t//!   part of the v1 target build.\n53\t//! * The `PARSE_*`/`IS_*_STREAM_ID(_*)` macros that the C\n54\t//!   header inlines as preprocessor macros are translated to\n55\t//!   `pub const fn` helpers.\n56\t\n57\tuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\n58\tuse std::fs::File;\n59\tuse std::path::PathBuf;\n60\t\n61\tuse core::any::Any;\n62\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n63\t\n64\tuse crate::arena::{Arena, Token};\n65\tuse crate::hash::{HashTable, HashToken};\n66\tuse crate::splay::{SplayToken, SplayTree};\n67\tuse crate::{Duration, Instant};\n68\t\n69\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` connection arena.\n70\t///\n71\t/// Phase 4 plan: every C `*mut picoquic_cnx_t` becomes a\n72\t/// [`ConnectionToken`].  Following it requires `quic.connections.get(tok)`\n73\t/// — one indirection through the arena, plus a generation check.\n74\t/// Stable across operations on other connections.\n75\tpub type ConnectionToken = Token<Connection>;\n76\t\n77\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` registered-token replay-protection arena.\n78\tpub type RegisteredTokenToken = Token<RegisteredToken>;\n79\t\n80\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` issued-tickets arena (server-side replay state).\n81\tpub type IssuedTicketToken = Token<IssuedTicket>;\n82\t\n83\t/// Token into the per-`Connection` (or per-`StreamHead`) stream-related\n84\t/// arenas.  Phase 4 may further split these into per-collection types.\n85\tpub type StreamToken = Token<StreamHead>;\n86\tpub type StreamDataToken = Token<StreamDataNode>;\n87\tpub type PacketToken = Token<Packet>;\n88\tpub type SackItemToken = Token<SackItem>;\n89\tpub type LocalConnectionIdToken = Token<LocalConnectionId>;\n90\tpub type PathToken = Token<Path>;\n91\tuse crate::logger::Logger;\n92\tuse crate::{\n93\t    AlpnSelect, CongestionAlgorithm, ConnectionId, ConnectionIdCallback, Fuzz, LossbitVersion,\n94\t    PacketContext, PathStatus, PmtudPolicy, RESET_SECRET_SIZE, SpinbitVersion, State,\n95\t    StreamDataCallback, StreamDirectReceive, TransportParameters,\n96\t};\n97\t\n98\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n99\t// Tunable constants (the `#define`s at the top of the C header).\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019hJ3usbndovtpVpSYaBo87","session_id":"c6df50c8-84e7-456d-b33a-aec683aa6926","uuid":"61a5191b-1c72-4c22-bad0-c907ee1e1560","timestamp":"2026-05-05T17:25:12.466Z"}
