ncast_mut`, so I need to dereference to get a mutable reference to the trait object and call `downcast_mut` on that instead. Writing setter methods...\n\nNow I need to verify that adding these new fields to the Quic struct won't break anything. I've already confirmed there are no struct literal constructions of Quic anywhere in the codebase, so it's safe to add the fields. Let me think through what else might need updating.\n\nSince the tls_api.rs functions will actually read and write these fields, clippy shouldn't complain about them being unused. Now I'll start implementing the changes: adding the fields to the Quic struct definition, fixing the doc comments, implementing the function bodies properly, replacing the remaining todo!() calls, and updating the related documentation in packet_loop.rs.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1786,"cache_read_input_tokens":149396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1786},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6df50c8-84e7-456d-b33a-aec683aa6926","uuid":"19b8bff2-6836-4143-bca5-27533679487e"}
